    <div class="container">
        <h1 class="section-title">History & Heritage</h1>
        
        <p>The Kasimid Sultanate, established on July 25, 2025, is a sovereign micronation located within Central New Jersey. It succeeds the legacy of the Raritan Caliphate.</p>
        <br>
        
        <h3>Etymology</h3>
        <p>The name is derived from the dynasty’s ancestor, Kasim al-Raniri, a semi-nomadic trader from the Maldives. The term “Kasimid” refers to the dynasty established in his name.</p>
        <br>

        <h3>Origins</h3>
        <p>The earliest inhabitants of our region were the Lenape tribes. Modern settlement began in 1988, with significant development in Ghabaani Province occurring in 1992. Following the dissolution of the Raritan Caliphate due to structural reforms, Yusuf I established the new Sultanate with a ratified Constitution.</p>
        <br>

        <h3>Culture</h3>
        <p>Our culture is a blend of Islamic values and maritime trade heritage. We observe holidays such as Eid al-Fitr, the Festival of Fragrance (Spring), and the Date Harvest Festival (Early Summer).</p>
    </div>

